WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:07.500
In this walkthrough we'll follow trading activity
into the accounting ledger, in the OpenTRMS Workbench.

2
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:17.100
Every trade eventually becomes an accounting entry.
The Journal List is where those entries live, and it
is the bridge between the trading floor and the ledger.

3
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:27.600
Entries carry a type. Mark to market records a
change in value, realized profit and loss
records a gain or loss that has actually crystallised.

4
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:38.000
Status matters just as much. A draft entry has
been generated but not committed to the ledger,
and only posted entries count towards the accounts.

5
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:47.900
The filters answer the two questions people
actually ask — what happened in this accounting
period, and what did this particular deal generate.

6
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:57.000
Opening an entry shows its lines.
Every entry balances, so the lines
always show a debit against a matching credit.

7
00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:08.933
None of this is typed by hand. Posting Rules is the
configuration that generates it — for each product and
entry type, which account is debited and which is credited.

8
00:01:08.933 --> 00:01:17.500
That completes Journals and Posting Rules. Every
surface shown here can also be opened from the agent
panel on the right, by asking for it in plain English.
